@startuml CryptoWeb-state-07-ledger-commit-action
title CryptoWeb - Ledger Commit Action Lifecycle

!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 65
skinparam ranksep 65
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam StateFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
hide empty description

state "IN_PROGRESS" as InProgress
state "SUCCESS" as Success
state "FAILED" as Failed

[*] --> InProgress : begin settlement or audit commit
InProgress --> Success : completed or no new records
InProgress --> Failed : lock contention or commit error
Failed --> InProgress : retry using same idempotency key
Success --> Success : repeat request / return previous result

note left of Success
  SUCCESS is the action outcome.
  A request with no uncommitted
  records can also succeed without
  creating a new block.
end note

note left of Failed
  Commit errors are recorded for
  inspection and retry. This is the
  state of the administrative action,
  not a trade-fill status.
end note

@enduml
